    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7218" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cautēr</span></b> , ēris,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καυτήρ</span> (accessory
		form to cauterium, and only post-class.). <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A branding-iron</i>, <i><span class="en">Pall.
				1, 41, 2</span></i>; <i><span class="en">1, 43, 3</span></i>; Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 10, 490.—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cauterem adigere ambitioni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tert. Pall. 5</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A wound made by burning</i>, Prud. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στεφ</span>. 5, 229.</div>
